torical decisions of many home buyers, curated by industry experts.   \nDwello, for every home buyer, is a way to go from 'I feel' to 'I know', at no extra cost.\n\n© 2023 JM Financial Products Limited. All Rights Reserved.](/home-lane)","images":[]},{"url":"https://www.squareyards.com/mumbai-residential-property/k-mehta-om-samarpan/100815/project","title":"K Mehta Om Samarpan, Borivali West, Mumbai - Price Starts from ₹1.51 Cr Onwards | 2, 3 BHK Flats Available","raw_content":"![Squareyards Logo](/assets/images/squareyards.png?aio=w-82;h-32;crop;)\n![K Mehta and Company developer logo](https://static.squareyards.com/resources/images/developerlogo/k-mehta-and-company-9553.jpg?aio=w-128;h-128;crop;)\n\n# K Mehta Om Samarpan Borivali West, Mumbai\n\n**₹1.51 Cr - 2.20 Cr**\n\n₹25,550 Per Sq. Ft.\n\n## Why Invest Through Square Yards?\n\n![Zero brokerage icon](/assets/images/zero-brokerage.svg)\n\n### Zero Brokerage\n\n100% Service, 0% Brokerage\n\n![Lowest price icon](/assets/images/lowest-price.svg)\n\n### Lowest Price Guaranteed\n\nHighly unlikely, but if you find a lower price anywhere, tell us and we will match it.\n\n![Full service support icon](/assets/images/full-service-support.svg)\n\n### Full Service Support\n\nOur sales personnel are accountable for every step.\n\n## About K Mehta Om Samarpan, Borivali West by K Mehta and Company\n\n## K Mehta Om Samarpan Price List, Price Trends and Market Insights\n\n### Price List\n\nView the latest price list for K Mehta Om Samarpan.\n\n| Unit Type (Carpet) | Price\\* | Action |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 2 BHK Apartment  606 Sq. Ft. | **₹ 1.51 Cr** | Check Availability |\n| 2 BHK Apartment  725 Sq. Ft. | **₹ 1.81 Cr** | Check Availability |\n| 3 BHK Apartment  812 Sq. Ft. | **₹ 2.00 Cr** | Check Availability |\n| 3 BHK Apartment  893 Sq. Ft. | **₹ 2.20 Cr** | Check Availability |\n\n\\*Prices are indicative and subject to applicable charges and project terms.\n\n### Price Trends\n\nK Mehta Om Samarpan's average asking price is stable quarter-on-quarter, compared with Borivali West.\n\nSep 2025 — Jun 2026\n\n| Quarter | K Mehta Om Samarpan | Borivali West |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Jun 2026 | 25550 | 30900 |\n| Mar 2026 | 25350 | 31300 |\n| Dec 2025 | 25500 | 30300 |\n| Sep 2025 | 37600 | 30350 |\n\n### Comparable Projects\n\nK Mehta Om Samarpan avg. price is ₹ 25.6 K/Sq.Ft. compared to Borivali West at ₹ 30.9 K/Sq.Ft.\n\n| Project | Avg. ₹/sq ft |\n| --- | --- |\n| [Dosti Oro 67](https://www.squareyards.com/mumbai-residential-property/dosti-oro-67/105339/project \"Dosti Oro 67\") | ₹ 31,100 |\n| Borivali West | ₹ 30,900 |\n| [Paradigm Revive](https://www.squareyards.com/mumbai-residential-property/paradigm-revive/107077/project \"Paradigm Revive\") | ₹ 28,050 |\n| Current Project **K Mehta Om Samarpan** | ₹ 25,550 |\n| [Shapoorji Pallonji Sarova Complex](https://www.squareyards.com/mumbai-residential-property/shapoorji-pallonji-sarova-complex/119475/project \"Shapoorji Pallonji Sarova Complex\") | ₹ 21,800 |\n\n### Rentals\n\nMonthly Rent in Borivali West ranges from ₹ 22.1 K to ₹ 74.4 K with options available for STUDIO,1,2,3 BHK units\n\n| Configuration | In K Mehta Om Samarpan | In Borivali West |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 BHK | - | ₹ 32.7 K |\n| 2 BHK | - | ₹ 45.5 K |\n| 3 BHK | - | ₹ 74.4 K |\n\n### Recent Updates\n\nGet the latest price and market updates for K Mehta Om Samarpan.\n\n#### MMRDA Plans Two New Ring Roads to Ease Mumbai Traffic\n\nThe Mumbai Metropolitan Region Development Authority (MMRDA) is planning two additional ring routes, expanding its proposed network from seven to nine. These new corridors will cover approximately 307 km and will connect existing roads and planned projects across Mumbai, Thane, and Navi Mumbai.\n\n#### Thane Infrastructure and Development Updates\n\nThe Thane-Borivali Twin Tunnel project saw the launch of TBM Arjuna on August 13, 2026, aiming to reduce travel time between Thane and Borivali to approximately 15 minutes. Amazon Data Services is developing a large data center in Ambernath, with an estimated construction cost of ₹3,500 crore, to be ready by 2029\n\n#### Mumbai Boosts Connectivity with Santacruz - Chembur link road Phase 2 & Chembur Metro Station\n\nCM Devendra Fadnavis inaugurated Phase 2 of the Santacruz-Chembur Link Road (SCLR) & the Chembur Metro Station under Metro Line 2B,The SCLR Phase 2 is expected to strengthen the road network between Mumbai's western and eastern suburbs, improving east-west connectivity.\n\n#### Thane-Borivali Twin Tunnel Project: Traffic Diversions Announced in Kasarvadavali\n\nTemporary traffic diversions have been implemented in Kasarvadavali for the ongoing work on the ambitious Thane-Borivali twin tunnel project by the Mumbai Metropolitan Region Development Authority (MMRDA). Certain routes will be closed from July 6 to August 5, 2026, to facilitate construction.\n\n#### Mumbai Monorail Services to Resume After Nine-Month Hiatus\n\nMumbai's monorail services are set to resume soon after a nine-month suspension, following approval from the Maharashtra government for safety improvements and fare revisions. MMRDA has proposed increased ticket prices. The monorail, which previously carried around 18,000 passengers daily, will offer improved services after safety upgrades.\n\nDuring Q2'2026, average property prices for K Mehta Om Samarpan moved from ₹ 25,350/sqft to ₹ 25,550/sqft, reflecting a 0.79% rise.\n\n#### MMRDA Presents Surplus Budget with Significant Allocation for Infrastructure\n\nMMRDA has presented a surplus budget of ₹48,072 crore, with 87% allocated to infrastructure projects, including roads, public transport, and urban development. A notable provision of ₹4,000 crore is earmarked for the development of Mumbai 3.0 New Town, aiming for planned urban expansion.\n\n#### BMC Budget Includes ₹6,475 Crore for Water Security Projects\n\nThe BMC's FY26-27 budget includes a substantial allocation of ₹6,475 crore for water security initiatives. This funding is designated for projects such as the Manori desalination plant (₹500 crore) and the Gargai project (₹437.51 crore), aimed at augmenting the city's water supply capacity.\n\n#### BMC Budget Includes ₹6,475 Crore for Water Security Projects\n\nThe BMC's FY26-27 budget includes a substantial allocation of ₹6,475 crore for water security initiatives. This funding is designated for projects such as the Manori desalination plant (₹500 crore) and the Gargai project (₹437.51 crore), aimed at augmenting the city's water supply capacity.\n\n#### Mumbai-Pune Expressway 'Missing Link' Project Set for May 1 Inauguration, Promising Safer and Faster Travel\n\nThe highly anticipated 'Missing Link' project on the Mumbai-Pune Expressway is set to be inaugurated on May 1, significantly reducing travel time by approximately 30 minutes and enhancing safety. The 10.5-km stretch features tunnels and a bridge, bypassing the accident-prone Khandala Ghat. This infrastructure upgrade is expected to ease traffic congestion, improve travel safety.\n\n## K Mehta Om Samarpan Floor Plans\n\n![Representative image for Floor plan of 2 BHK 606 Sq. Ft. Apartment in K Mehta Om Samarpan, Mumbai](/assets/images/floor-plans-coming-soon.svg)\n\nPrice:₹ 1.51 Cr\n\n![Representative image for Floor plan of 2 BHK 725 Sq. Ft. Apartment in K Mehta Om Samarpan, Mumbai](/assets/images/floor-plans-coming-soon.svg)\n\nPrice:₹ 1.81 Cr\n\n![Representative image for Floor plan of 3 BHK 812 Sq. Ft. Apartment in K Mehta Om Samarpan, Mumbai](/assets/images/floor-plans-coming-soon.svg)\n\nPrice:₹ 2.00 Cr\n\n![Representative image for Floor plan of 3 BHK 893 Sq. Ft. Apartment in K Mehta Om Samarpan, Mumbai](/assets/images/floor-plans-coming-soon.svg)\n\nPrice:₹ 2.20 Cr\n\n## Amenities & Specifications of K Mehta Om Samarpan\n\n### Sports Sports\n\n![Sports](https://static.squareyards.com/assets/images/svg/amenities/sports/am-ico-gymnasiu-active.svg)\n\n### Convenience Convenience\n\n![Convenience](https://static.squareyards.com/assets/images/svg/amenities/convenience/am-ico-powerbac-active.svg)\n\n### Safety Safety\n\n![Safety](https://static.squareyards.com/assets/images/svg/amenities/safety/am-ico-24x7secu-active.svg)\n\n### Leisure Leisure\n\n![Leisure](https://static.squareyards.com/assets/images/svg/amenities/leisure/am-ico-clubhous-active.svg)\n\n### Environment Environment\n\n![Environment](https://static.squareyards.com/assets/images/svg/amenities/environment/am-ico-normalpa-active.svg)\n\n### Specifications\n\n## Location and Connectivity Around K Mehta and Company Borivali West\n\n![Connectivity map showing nearby places around Mumbai Western Suburbs](/assets/images/project-map.png?aio=w-714;h-317;crop;)\n\nEstimate commute from your office or kid's school to K Mehta Om Samarpan.\n\n![Car travel mode](/assets/images/car-fill.svg)\n\nPlease select the starting point to calculate the travel time.\n\n![Rolling loader icon](/assets/images/rolling-loader.gif)\n\n### Nearby Landmarks\n\n#### Gokhale Education Society Shishu Vikas Mandir\n\n#### Ganesh Mandir Kastur Park\n\n#### Vibha Care Home - The Family Hospital\n\n### Connecting Roads\n\nAverage Asking Price in Borivali West\n\nBased on active listings and recent trends\n\nWestern Express Highway & SV Road\n\nLimited social amenities and infrastructure\n\nBorivali West attracts me since my experiences feel subdued and balanced. Nearby markets daily and excellent schools are good. Weekend beach time and runs close to SGNP are something I like. Andheri and Goregaon are simple for me to work in. Parking problems and traffic jams call for quick solutions.\n\n— Suresh Sanghvi, Tenant\n\n## RERA Details of K Mehta Om Samarpan\n\n## How does K Mehta Om Samarpan compare with similar projects?\n\n![K Mehta Om Samarpan project in Borivali West, Mumbai](https://static.squareyards.com/resources/images/mumbai/tn-projectflagship/tn-k-mehta-om-samarpan-project-flagship1.jpg?aio=w-229;h-150;crop;)\n\n### [K Mehta Om Samarpan](https://www